Lojban quarterly journal published by ((The Logical Language Group)).

Initially published in July 1986 as "((me la uacintyn loglytuan))'', a newletter serving a Washington D.C. ((Loglan)) special interest group (SIG), it assumed a broader mandate in 1987 and was renamed "((hoi loglypli))" in 1987. In February 1988, it was renamed "ju'i lobypli". Like "hoi loglypli", this meant "hey, loglan user", but it used a new public domain vocabulary owing to copyright claims pressed by ((The Loglan Institute)).

18 issues appeared between July 1986 and June 1993. Two formatted versions are available on ((mw:zo'ei la'e "lu ju'i lobypli li'u"|the lojban mediawiki)):

* ((mw: me lu ju'i lobypli li'u 4 moi | Number 4 - February 1988)) 
* ((mw: me lu ju'i lobypli li'u 5 moi | Number 5 - May 1988)) 

Unformatted versions are available at the Lojban web site: [http://www.lojban.org/files/jl/]